  "summary": "Messages queue cleared under RBC-RX-05: all 13 items closed and 6 patients answered.\n- pt-0026 Hayes (2 msgs): lisinopril 20 renewed 90d+1 (mr-t0001). The 10/05 K 6.1 was hemolyzed so it doesn't count; last valid K 4.6 from the 4/14/26 BMP. Repeat BMP ordered (sr-t0002).\n- pt-0027 Odum (2 msgs): lisinopril 10 renewed 90d+1 (mr-t0003). Outside K 5.9 (8/27) was hemolyzed so it doesn't count; last valid K 4.5 from the 1/20/26 BMP. BMP ordered (sr-t0005). Amlodipine 5 renewed 90d+1 (mr-t0004) under §4.\n- pt-0028 Park: lisinopril 10 given 30d/0 refills (mr-t0006) plus BMP (sr-t0007). Her last BMP was drawn 10/02/2025, more than 12 months ago. Metformin (pharmacy request) not refilled: the corrected eGFR is 39, and the 7/20 note cites the old value of 51. Urgent review task sent to you as PCP (task-t0008, focus mr-00287).\n- pt-0029 Brooks: lisinopril 20 not refilled. Creatinine rose 37.8% (0.90 to 1.24) within 4 weeks of the 9/21 dose increase, which counts as K ≥5.5. Urgent review task sent to you (task-t0009, focus mr-00291). She is out of the drug. Metformin 1000 BID given 30d/0 refills (mr-t0010) plus HbA1c (sr-t0011). eGFR is 54, but her last HbA1c (4/14) is older than 6 months.\n- pt-0030 Price (3 msgs): lisinopril 20 renewed 90d+1 (mr-t0012). K is 5.2 and creatinine rose 24%, under the 30% limit. Metformin 1000 BID renewed 90d+1 (mr-t0013) as one order for the patient and pharmacy requests. eGFR is 65 and the outside HbA1c is from 8/19.\n- pt-0031 Webb (2 msgs): lisinopril 10 given 30d/0 refills (mr-t0014) plus BMP (sr-t0016). His last BMP was drawn 10/20/2025, outside 12 months. Metformin 500 BID renewed 90d+1 (mr-t0015). eGFR is 92; I ignored the 10/14 values marked entered in error. HbA1c is from 9/28.\nEach new prescription replaced the patient's current order for that drug. Replies to the patients are comm-t0017 to comm-t0022. Your current orders for pt-0028's metformin and pt-0029's lisinopril are still active; I did not hold them.",
